.\"  -*- nroff -*-
.Dd October 16, 2026
.Dt MCTL 8 SMM
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mctl
.Nd status tool for
.Xr mcd 8
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl hmptv
.Op Fl i Ar NAME
.Op Fl u Ar FILE
.Op Ar COMMAND
.Nm
.Fl C Ar WORD...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
queries a running
.Xr mcd 8
over its IPC socket and shows the queriers, the group memberships and
the multicast state of the bridge.  Without a command it runs
.Cm show .
.Pp
Most bridge state comes from the iproute2 tools
.Xr ip 8
and
.Xr bridge 8 ,
and from
.Xr jq 1 .
Their BusyBox versions are not enough, use
.Cm check
to confirm.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , -help
Show usage and, when
.Nm mcd
is running, the available commands.
.It Fl i , -ident Ns = Ns Ar NAME
Talk to an
.Nm mcd
started with the same
.Fl i Ar NAME .
.It Fl m , -monitor
Run the command every two seconds, like
.Xr watch 1 .
.It Fl p , -plain
Plain table headings, no terminal control characters.  Implied for
JSON output.
.It Fl t , -no-heading
Skip table headings.
.It Fl u , -ipc Ns = Ns Ar FILE
IPC socket, default derived from the identity.  Also settable with the
.Ev MCD_SOCK
environment variable.
.It Fl v , -version
Show version and exit.
.It Fl C , -complete Ar WORD...
Used by the shell completion scripts.  Prints the candidates for the
last word, which may be partial, from the running daemon's command
list, one per line.  Prints nothing when no daemon is running.
.El
.Pp
Output width follows the terminal.
.Pp
Completion scripts for
.Xr bash 1
and
.Xr zsh 1
are installed with
.Nm .
The commands come from the running daemon, so they are not completed
while it is down.
.Sh COMMANDS
Commands can be abbreviated, e.g.\&
.Cm s i
for
.Cm show interfaces .
Adding
.Cm json
to a
.Cm show
command gives machine readable output.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm show Oo Cm igmp Oc Op Cm json
Overview: global settings, bridge port roles, the queriers and the
group memberships.  In JSON the queriers are split in
.Dq multicast-queriers
for IGMP and
.Dq mld-queriers
for MLD.
.It Cm show status Op Cm json
Global settings.
.It Cm show interfaces Op Cm json
One row per interface and protocol: VLAN, protocol, elected querier,
state, query interval, querier timeout and protocol version.  The
JSON output also has the interface's
.Cm router-timeout ,
the other querier present interval.
.It Cm show groups Op Cm json
IGMP and MLD group memberships, as seen by the bridge.
.It Cm show router-ports Op Cm json
Multicast router ports, grouped per bridge.
.It Cm show routers Op Cm json
Multicast routers heard through Multicast Router Discovery, RFC 4286,
per interface and protocol: address, advertisement interval, query
interval, robustness and seconds until the entry expires.  An entry
goes when its router sends a termination, or after three advertisement
intervals of silence.  Routers are heard whether or not
.Cm mrd
is on for the interface.
.It Cm show mdb
The bridge multicast forwarding database, as
.Ql bridge mdb show
but readable.
.It Cm check
Verify that the tools listed above are available.
.It Cm version
Show the version of the running
.Nm mcd .
.It Cm help
List the commands the running
.Nm mcd
supports.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width MCD_SOCK
.It Ev MCD_SOCK
IPC socket path, overridden by
.Fl u .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /run/mcd.sock -compact
.It Pa /run/mcd.sock
Default IPC socket, follows the identity.  The group owner is set at
build time, see
.Ql configure --with-group .
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ mctl show interfaces
Interface       VID  Proto  Querier                      State  Interval  Timeout  MRD  Ver
vlan1                IGMP   192.168.1.1                     Up       125     None   on    3
vlan1                MLD    fe80::7a4c:9bff:fe12:3456       Up       125     None   on    2
br0              42  IGMP   0.0.0.0                         Up       125     None  off    3
br0              42  MLD    ::                              Up       125     None  off    2
.Ed
.Pp
The IPC protocol is plain text, one command per connection, so other
programs can use it directly:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
echo "show igmp json" | socat - UNIX-CONNECT:/run/mcd.sock
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mcd.conf 5 ,
.Xr mcd 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An -nosplit
